@cc [owner:id13,label:security;concurrency] bounded-live-metadata
Live mounts MUST validate metadata, including selected revision, namespace entries and authority, after one second measured from validation request start. Cache hits and delayed replies MUST NOT renew that deadline. Failed refresh MUST NOT serve expired observations. Immutable bytes MAY remain cached beyond expiry only when validated metadata still selects their revision and allows access. Existing descriptors MUST retain identity across unlink or rename-over and follow the current revision after validation. Mmap MUST NOT be represented as a live view.

@cc [owner:id13,label:backend;concurrency] optimistic-live-publication
Cached revisions MAY supply speculative write preconditions even after their observation deadline, provided publication itself validates them authoritatively; expired metadata MUST NOT be served by reads or stat. The server MUST check original revision, entry tokens and current authority atomically with publication. A conflict MUST NOT silently rebase the rejected payload. Ambiguous outcomes MUST retain original request identity and payload across descriptor closure. Installing an acknowledged local revision MUST NOT renew unrelated deadlines or skip unseen journal events.

@cc [owner:id13,label:backend;error-handling] live-durability-tracking
Live mounts MUST retain bounded publication receipts and ambiguous outcomes across descriptor close/reopen. Explicit fsync MUST resolve prior relevant outcomes and confirm their persistence. Close-time flush MUST check deferred errors without requiring another persistence barrier. Successful persistence confirmation MUST NOT renew metadata or authority. Capacity exhaustion MUST reject publication before losing its tracking obligation.

@cc [owner:id13,label:backend;concurrency] live-rocksdb-persistence-prefix
Clearing receipts for multiple objects after one RocksDB persistence barrier MUST occur only while client publications are excluded and after a confirmation in the same server incarnation. The server barrier MUST cover every publication acknowledged before the call. Tenant journal positions MUST NOT be compared numerically with engine persistence prefixes. This optimization MUST NOT be copied to an adapter whose barrier confirms only the supplied receipt.

@cc [owner:id13,label:security;concurrency] bounded-readdirplus-and-cached-reads
Readdirplus MUST use current authorized attributes within the original validation deadline and account for every kernel lookup reference actually returned. Refreshing directory continuation MUST refresh its attributes, not only its deadline. Synchronous cached reads MUST validate identity, revision and authority under the metadata deadline before replying; misses, expiry and concurrent validation MUST fall back to the bounded asynchronous path without serving expired data.

@cc [owner:id13,label:security;performance;concurrency] authorized-content-hash-cache
Manifest entries MUST bind a file revision and range; content-hashed bytes MUST remain private to the authenticated mount cache and MUST NOT confer authority. Batch reads MUST authorize every file/retained handle from one backend snapshot, bound request count and expanded chunk bytes, and isolate each range's error. Known hashes MAY suppress payload only for that authorized manifest. Clients MUST retain omitted bytes through the response, verify received digests and response identities/ranges/EOF, and revalidate revision and authority before serving or installing fetched entries. Metadata expiry MUST NOT evict immutable content. Combined content and manifest cache charges MUST stay within the configured content-cache budget; queues and admitted reads MUST remain bounded.

@cc [owner:id13,label:performance;concurrency] bounded-read-backpressure
When asynchronous FUSE content reads fill the configured admission capacity, the dispatcher MUST wait for a completion instead of returning EAGAIN solely because capacity is full. Outstanding daemon read tasks MUST remain bounded by that capacity; excess requests remain in the kernel queue or the dispatcher. Completion and shutdown MUST wake and drain waiters without requiring another FUSE callback.
